# Counting evaluation (MOT17)

Generated by `backend/eval/counting_eval.py`. Data: the second half of each MOT17 training sequence (boxmot
`MOT17-50` release). Ground truth = distinct pedestrian IDs (class 1, `consider` = 1). Predicted tracks that
spend most of their life on distractors (static people, cyclists, reflections) are not counted.
Detector: **vs2-y26n** at 640 px. Thresholds tuned on MOT17-02/04 (216 trials),
reported on sequences never used for tuning.

## Unique-person count error (lower is better)

| sequence | GT people | Naive: people per frame, 1 frame/s (v1) | ByteTrack, Ultralytics defaults | ByteTrack, tuned thresholds | Ours: tuned + confirmation + merge |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| MOT17-05 | 71 | 86 (21%) | 77 (8%) | 69 (3%) | 60 (15%) |
| MOT17-09 | 22 | 30 (36%) | 38 (73%) | 30 (36%) | 27 (23%) |
| MOT17-10 | 36 | 16 (56%) | 35 (3%) | 32 (11%) | 24 (33%) |
| MOT17-11 | 44 | 62 (41%) | 44 (0%) | 38 (14%) | 33 (25%) |
| MOT17-13 | 44 | 10 (77%) | 22 (50%) | 19 (57%) | 14 (68%) |
| **mean error** | | **46.2%** | **26.8%** | **24.1%** | **32.9%** |

## Tracking quality

| sequence | IDF1 default | IDF1 ours | MOTA default | MOTA ours | ID switches default | ID switches ours |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| MOT17-05 | 0.424 | 0.400 | 0.320 | 0.292 | 56 | 43 |
| MOT17-09 | 0.503 | 0.504 | 0.461 | 0.422 | 40 | 21 |
| MOT17-10 | 0.216 | 0.205 | 0.127 | 0.110 | 21 | 14 |
| MOT17-11 | 0.527 | 0.538 | 0.514 | 0.471 | 18 | 13 |
| MOT17-13 | 0.166 | 0.138 | 0.078 | 0.061 | 8 | 1 |

MOTA is bounded by the detector (missed and false boxes); it is listed to show the tracker does not
trade detections for a better count.

## Chosen thresholds

```json
{
  "track_high_thresh": 0.3,
  "new_track_thresh": 0.25,
  "min_hits": 2,
  "min_age_s": 0.2,
  "min_hit_ratio": 0.5,
  "track_buffer_s": 1.5,
  "reid_window_s": 0.0
}
```

